This work incorporates and derives from the following.

1. Bonsai — a gravitational N-body tree code for GPUs
   Copyright the Bonsai authors: Jeroen Bedorf, Evghenii Gaburov and
   Simon Portegies Zwart.
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

   BanyanPM's tree construction, the warp-cooperative tree traversal, the device
   memory abstractions and the program skeleton derive directly from Bonsai. The
   code has been ported from CUDA to HIP and modified substantially: the force
   kernel, the time integration, the timestep criterion, the softening, the
   periodic TreePM split and the I/O have been rewritten to follow Gadget-2.

   As required by the Apache License 2.0 Section 4, this notice is retained and
   the files carry notice of modification. Apache-2.0 material may be relicensed
   under GPLv3 in a combined work; the combined work as distributed here is
   GPLv3.

2. GADGET-2 — a cosmological N-body/SPH simulation code
   Copyright Volker Springel.
   Released under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

   GADGET-2 is the REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION that BanyanPM's physics is modelled
   on and validated against. Its algorithms were reimplemented here: the
   opening criteria, the spline softening, the drift and kick factor tables,
   the individual timestep criterion, the TreePM short/long-range split and the
   snapshot and parameter-file formats. Source locations in GADGET-2 are cited
   throughout the code comments so that any behaviour can be checked against the
   original.

   Volker Springel is not an author of BanyanPM and has no involvement in it.
